From: Kernel audit <littleddfu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: em_meta: bound the shift exponent for integer metadata

meta_int_apply_extras() shifts an unsigned long by a value taken verbatim
from userspace:

	static void meta_int_apply_extras(struct meta_value *v,
					  struct meta_obj *dst)
	{
		if (v->hdr.shift)
			dst->value >>= v->hdr.shift;

v->hdr is a copy of the user-supplied struct tcf_meta_val, whose shift
field is a __u8, so it ranges over 0..255.  em_meta_change() validates
only TCF_META_TYPE() and TCF_META_ID() and that the id has a ->get; the
shift is never bounded, here or anywhere else.  The variable-length
sibling meta_var_apply_extras() *is* guarded with shift < dst->len, so
only the integer path is affected.

Shifting an unsigned long by BITS_PER_LONG or more is undefined:

  UBSAN: shift-out-of-bounds in net/sched/em_meta.c:766:14
  shift exponent 255 is too large for 64-bit type 'long unsigned int'
  Call Trace:
   __ubsan_handle_shift_out_of_bounds+0x2d4/0x2f0
   meta_int_apply_extras+0xf0/0x100
   meta_get+0x144/0x330
   em_meta_match+0x84/0x1c0
   __tcf_em_tree_match+0x15e/0x540
   basic_classify+0xed/0x220
   tcf_classify+0x31c/0x4d0
   prio_enqueue+0x146/0x4e0
   __dev_queue_xmit+0xeed/0x23d0

reached by attaching a cls_basic filter carrying an em_meta ematch with
shift = 255 and then transmitting through the qdisc.  An unprivileged
process can do this inside a user+net namespace.

Note this is undefined behaviour rather than memory corruption: on x86
the shift count is masked to 63, so the result is a wrong value, not an
out-of-bounds access.

Reject an out-of-range shift when the ematch is configured, so the filter
is refused with -EINVAL instead of producing UB on every packet.

diff --git a/net/sched/em_meta.c b/net/sched/em_meta.c
index 48bdd77df0a3..52a108257766 100644
--- a/net/sched/em_meta.c
+++ b/net/sched/em_meta.c
@@ -927,6 +927,16 @@ static int em_meta_change(struct net *net, void *data, int len,
 	    TCF_META_ID(hdr->right.kind) > TCF_META_ID_MAX)
 		goto errout;
 
+	/* For integer metadata the shift is applied to an unsigned long in
+	 * meta_int_apply_extras(), so anything from BITS_PER_LONG upwards is
+	 * undefined.  The variable-length variant is already bounded against
+	 * the value length in meta_var_apply_extras(); only this side is not.
+	 */
+	if (TCF_META_TYPE(hdr->left.kind) == TCF_META_TYPE_INT &&
+	    (hdr->left.shift >= BITS_PER_LONG ||
+	     hdr->right.shift >= BITS_PER_LONG))
+		goto errout;
+
 	meta = kzalloc_obj(*meta);
 	if (meta == NULL) {
 		err = -ENOMEM;
